<h1>Help</h1>
<p class="info-updated">Quick answers to the most common questions. Can’t find yours? Email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>

<h2>Trips</h2>
<details><summary>How do I plan a new trip?</summary>
  <p>Go to <a href="/groups">My Trips</a> and start a new trip: pick the country, the cities and how many days. You’ll get an invite link to share with your group.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do friends join my trip?</summary>
  <p>Send them the trip’s invite link. Once they’re signed in, opening the link adds them to the trip, its chat and its plans.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do recommendations and voting work?</summary>
  <p>In the trip’s Recommendations tab, everyone swipes through things to do: thumbs up, save for later, or dismiss. Upvoted and saved activities show up in the itinerary, ready to drag into a day.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I build the itinerary?</summary>
  <p>In the Itinerary tab, pick your start and end dates on the calendar, then drag activities onto the times you want. On a phone, press and hold an activity to drag it, or tap it and then tap a time. Everyone in the trip sees changes straight away.</p></details>
<details><summary>What’s in the Destination tab?</summary>
  <p>The local time and weather, the forecast for each trip day (or the typical weather when the trip is more than two weeks away), public holidays, places that are closed on your dates, and a map of where it’s likely to be busy. Crowds are an estimate, and opening hours come from OpenStreetMap, so check important places before you go.</p></details>

<h2>Friends</h2>
<details><summary>How do I add a friend?</summary>
  <p>Open <a href="/friends">Friends</a> and search by name or exact email, then tap Add friend. When they accept, you can see each other’s visited countries and planned trips.</p></details>
<details><summary>What can people who aren’t my friends see?</summary>
  <p>Only your name, your profile photo and how many friends you have.</p></details>

<h2>Your account</h2>
<details><summary>I forgot my password</summary>
  <p>Use <a href="/auth/forgot-password">Forgot password</a> on the log-in page and we’ll email you a link to set a new one.</p></details>
<details><summary>I didn’t get the verification code</summary>
  <p>Check your spam folder, then try logging in again: an account that isn’t verified yet gets a fresh code.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I delete my account?</summary>
  <p>Go to <a href="/settings">Settings</a> › Delete Account. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for what’s removed.</p></details>
